    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0202" n="190" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg190"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation(2)/41: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-21T16:00:00-03:00">June 21, 1940—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 21—3:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>297. For the Under Secretary. My 291, June 18, 5 p.m. Aranha showed me a telegram
                    this morning from his Ambassador at Buenos Aires reporting that Cantilo<anchor
                        n="17" xml:id="d246-f1"/> told him that Espil<anchor n="18" xml:id="d246-f2"
                    /> reports that a 5-point program (which he described) is under discussion for
                    the agenda of the conference which will be called for June 26. Aranha expressed
                    surprise at the breadth of the program and remarked that the 26th would allow
                    very little time for study of so many important subjects.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d246-f1" n="17" xml:id="d246-f1-content">
                <p>José María Cantilo, Argentine Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d246-f2" n="18" xml:id="d246-f2-content">
                <p>Felipe A. Espil, Argentine Ambassador in the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
